# ==============================================================================
# Lifeline Static Hardware-to-IP Table (/etc/lifeline/dhcp_hosts.csv)
# ==============================================================================
# Format:
#   mac,ipv4,hostname,ipv6_host
#
# Fields:
#   mac       : Client Ethernet MAC address (aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff, case-insensitive)
#   ipv4      : Static IPv4 address inside [lan].eth_ip's subnet (must != eth_ip)
#   hostname  : Optional DNS hostname registered in dnsmasq (may be blank)
#   ipv6_host : Optional IPv6 host suffix inside [lan].eth_ipv6_prefix (e.g.
#               "::101"). If blank, defaults to "::<last_ipv4_octet>" so
#               192.168.9.101 automatically maps to <ULA_PREFIX>::101.
#
# Tip for multi-laptop setups (up to 5 laptops sharing one switch):
#   If you ALSO want a laptop whose Wi-Fi fails (FAILOVER mode) to receive an
#   address from whichever laptop is currently PRIMARY, list all laptops'
#   Ethernet MACs in this table alongside your client devices!
# ==============================================================================

aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:01,192.168.9.101,device-alpha,
aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:02,192.168.9.102,device-beta,::102
aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:03,192.168.9.103,sensor-rig,
